From e860f69c624a2a7ec9312751ff2306165a539ec6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 16:54:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 238/252] fix(execution): anchor request dtype/rank checks and
 fallback chain structure

0042 item 1b2, from the verifier's remaining ledger:

- selected candidate checks are now authoritative by stable check name:
  detail.requested of the rank check must equal len(request.left_shape), and
  request.dtype must belong to the selected provider's declared dtype tuple
  (or the registered contract domain); missing/duplicated selected checks and
  a missing/duplicated selected candidate fail closed
- non-selected candidates' checks stay an explanation layer (they may be
  rejected before the rank/dtype checks run), so genuine vendor/fallback
  reports keep validating
- resolution.fallback_chain must be non-empty and unique and
  chain[chain_position] must be the invoked provider; a genuine AOCL runtime
  fallback report (declared f32, invoked portable, position 1) validates
- rewrite the binding_verify normative/explanation/boundary statement, and
  mirror it in the report validator comment
